   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 192 of the laws of 2011, relating to authorizing certain health care professionals licensed to practice in other jurisdictions to practice in this state in connection with an event sanctioned by New York Road Runners, in relation to extending the provisions thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S2762",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2762-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Chap 192 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Health",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2762\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 192 of the laws of 2011,\nrelating to authorizing certain health care professionals licensed to\npractice in other jurisdictions to practice in this state in\nconnection with an event sanctioned by New York Road Runners, in\nrelation to extending the provisions thereof\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo authorize certain licensed health care professionals from other\njurisdictions to practice in New York State with respect to six major\nevents sanctioned by New York Road Runners.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1-Authorizes that any person who is licensed to practice as a\nphysician, physician's assistant, massage therapist, physical\ntherapist, chiropractor, dentist, optometrist, nurse, nurse\npractitioner, certified athletic trainer or podiatrist in another\nstate or territory, who is in good standing in such state or territory\nand who has been appointed by the New York Road Runners to provide\nprofessional services at an event in this state sanctioned by the New\nYork Road Runners, may provide such professional services to athletes\nand team personnel registered to train at a location in this state or\nregistered to compete in an event conducted under the sanction of the\nNew York Road Runners in the state without first being licensed\npursuant to the provisions of Title 8 of the Education Law. Such\nservices may be provided only four days before the following events,\nduring the following events, and one day after the following events:\n\nEvent                                        Date\n\n\nStaten Island Half                           10.08.2017\nNew York City Marathon                       11.05.2017\nBrooklyn Half                                05.20.2017\nBronx Half                                   09.24.2017\nQueens 10K                                   06.17.2017\nNew York City Half                           03.19.2017\n\nSection 2-Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThere are not enough health care professionals available, within the\nState of New York, to meet the needs of participants in certain major\nevents sanctioned by the New York Road Runners, including the New York\nCity Marathon. Accordingly, it would be advantageous to allow licensed\nhealth care professionals, who are in good standing with their\nrespective state or territory, to provide such services here in New\nYork.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is effectively a one year extender of legislation that has\nhistorically passed each year, such as Chapter 39 of the Laws of 2016.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately and shall expire and be deemed repealed January 31, 2018.\n",
